  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $5.9B in FY2027 to date. The agency recorded 12,835 awards with an average award size of $457K. Obligations are down 93.5% year over year. Fiscal-year comparisons show a steep decline relative to prior years, which ranged from $56.4B in FY22 up to $90.6B in FY26, then $5.9B in FY27. The top spending categories in FY2027 to date are dominated by health and medical services plus construction, telecommunications, and IT. The largest individual vendor is TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP at $900M, followed by several medical services and technology firms. This snapshot reflects partial-year totals, so FY2027 totals remain fiscal year to date and not final.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How big is VA's FY2027 contract activity?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $5.9B in FY2027 to date. The Department of Veterans Affairs made 12,835 awards with an average award size of $457K. Obligations are down 93.5% year over year. Prior-year totals were $56.4B in FY22, $61.7B in FY23, $66.9B in FY24, $78.3B in FY25, and $90.6B in FY26."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where does the money go in FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers received $1.1B in obligations. Offices of Physicians (except Mental Health Specialists) received $453M and Commercial and Institutional Building Construction received $433M. Wired Telecommunications Carriers, Computer Systems Design Services, and Other Computer Related Services received $322M, $286M, and $260M respectively."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Department of Veterans Affairs spend on contracts?",
      "a": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $5.9B in FY2027 to date. The Department of Veterans Affairs recorded 12,835 awards with an average award size of $457K, and obligations are down 93.5% year over year."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Veterans Affairs buy?",
      "a": "The Department of Veterans Affairs's top NAICS categories in FY2027 to date include Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers ($1.1B); Offices of Physicians (except Mental Health Specialists) ($453M); Commercial and Institutional Building Construction ($433M); Wired Telecommunications Carriers ($322M); Computer Systems Design Services ($286M); Other Computer Related Services ($260M); Analytical Laboratory Instrument Manufacturing ($179M); Couriers and Express Delivery Services ($146M); Temporary Help Services ($132M); and Surgical and Medical Instrument Manufacturing ($123M)."
    },
    {
      "q": "Who are Veterans Affairs's largest contractors?",
      "a": "The Department of Veterans Affairs's top vendors in FY2027 to date are TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP ($900M), QTC MEDICAL SERVICES INC ($247M), AT&T ENTERPRISES, LLC ($226M), SIGNATURE CHOICE III, LLC ($226M), ACCENTURE FEDERAL SERVICES LLC ($151M), THUNDERCAT TECHNOLOGY, LLC ($150M), DELOITTE CONSULTING LLP ($142M), VETERANS EVALUATION SERVICES, INC ($97.4M), LUMEN TECHNOLOGIES GOVERNMENT SOLUTIONS, INC. ($93.4M), and MEDLINE INDUSTRIES, LP ($89.1M)."
